# Email template copy

Read [docs/email-templates/README.md](../../docs/email-templates/README.md) first.

## Source of truth

Plain-text copy for these six templates lives in:

- [docs/email-templates/en.md](../../docs/email-templates/en.md)
- [docs/email-templates/nl.md](../../docs/email-templates/nl.md)
- [docs/email-templates/fr.md](../../docs/email-templates/fr.md)

Edit the markdown files before changing seed or production rows.

## Seed and HTML

[`seed-email-templates.ts`](../../apps/api/src/mailer/seed-email-templates.ts) must match the markdown (`contentPlain` verbatim; `contentRich` as HTML with the same wording).

- Activation/login links: `<a href="{{url}}">…</a>` using the localized label from the md file.
- Contact line: `<a href="mailto:info@coderdojobelgium.be">info@coderdojobelgium.be</a>`
- Bullet lists in md → `<ul><li>…</li></ul>` in `contentRich`
- Keep Handlebars blocks (`{{#if …}}`) identical between plain and rich

## Do not

- Reintroduce FAQ URLs or `Go2MyProject`
- Use “copy between quotes” URL instructions
- Change copy in seed only without updating the matching `docs/email-templates/*.md`
